                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "As far as rhythm games go, this one is very simplistic. For a rhythm game, the levels are on the longer side, at around 15 minutes. However, the length of the levels doesn't feel particularly justified. While the levels gradually introduce more difficult patterns throughout, the core gameplay feels too simplistic for much of this variation to remain engaging. Some of the sections are interesting, and there's enough of a challenge that mastering the levels and improving your score could be fun, but overall there's not enough here to make me want to do that.",
